From a48e9add26e4fd7892ce0c25d353c794a0eccc21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:41:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bugfix: return the ordering status from
 `ParMETIS_V3_NodeND()` [report R. Perry]

`ParMETIS_V3_NodeND()` returned `METIS_OK` only when the separator
tree could be turned into the ParMETIS `sizes` array, that is, when
the number of processes is a power of two and a `sizes` array is
provided, although the ordering had been computed in all cases, as
documented. Conversely, the return values of
`SCOTCH_dgraphOrderCompute()` and `SCOTCH_dgraphOrderPerm()` were
ignored, so that a failed ordering was reported as a success.

The status now reflects the computation of the ordering only, and the
`sizes` array is filled on a best-effort basis, keeping its documented
-1 values when the number of processes is not a power of two. The test
program is run on three processes as well, and checks the `sizes`
array.

Refs: CLI-09
